---

<AudienceLanding {...page}>
  <section slot="before-challenge" class="section corporate-route-chooser" aria-labelledby="corporate-route-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading audience-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow dark">Choose your starting point</p><h2 id="corporate-route-title">What role do you want to play?</h2></div>
        <p>The same organisation can use both routes, but each has a different buyer, budget and first conversation. Choose the one closest to your priority now.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="corporate-route-grid">
        <a class="corporate-route-card route-cohort" href="#mission-cohort">
          <span>Route 01 · Fund impact</span><h3>Mission Cohort Partnership</h3>
          <p>Choose one mission. Equip a cohort of trusted social enterprises. Receive one clear report showing collective reach, outcomes and learning.</p>
          <strong>Explore sponsored cohorts <b aria-hidden="true">→</b></strong>
        </a>
        <a class="corporate-route-card route-direct" href="#ai-delivery-partnership">
          <span>Route 02 · Buy capability</span><h3>AI Coaching &amp; Delivery Partnership</h3>
          <p>Add safe guided-support capacity to your workforce, customers, operations or projects—with practical Responsible AI consultancy where needed.</p>
          <strong>Explore direct deployment <b aria-hidden="true">→</b></strong>
        </a>
      </div>
      <figure class="corporate-route-visual">
        <img src="/images/landing/corporate-two-routes.webp" alt="Social-enterprise and corporate teams connected through a shared mission, AI coaching and one view of impact" width="1672" height="941" loading="eager" />
        <figcaption>
          <span><b>01</b> Trusted organisations deliver locally</span>
          <span><b>02</b> Your teams add support capacity</span>
          <span><b>03</b> One connected impact story</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section slot="after-solution" class="section mission-cohort-offer" id="mission-cohort" aria-labelledby="mission-cohort-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading audience-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Route 01 · Mission Cohort Partnership</p><h2 id="mission-cohort-title">Fund one mission. Equip trusted organisations. See the impact clearly.</h2></div>
        <p>You choose a population, place, contract outcome or mission. Bridgit and SEUK shape a small cohort of relevant social enterprises around it, while each member keeps ownership of its local expertise and delivery.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mission-cohort-grid">
        <ol class="mission-cohort-steps">
          <li><span>01</span><div><h3>Choose the mission</h3><p>Start with care and health equity, secure homes and financial resilience, jobs and skills, community access or another defined outcome.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>02</span><div><h3>Design the cohort</h3><p>Identify two to five suitable social enterprises, the shared user journey, local configuration, safeguards and realistic budget route.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>03</span><div><h3>Deploy local coaches</h3><p>Each member receives configured AI coaching, onboarding, training and ongoing optimisation around its own service.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>04</span><div><h3>Report one impact story</h3><p>A common evidence framework brings member results into one sponsor view without flattening local differences.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
        <aside class="sponsor-report-card">
          <span>What you receive</span><h3>One sponsor report. Clear evidence underneath.</h3>
          <ul><li><strong>Reach</strong><small>Who accessed support and whether priority groups were reached</small></li><li><strong>Engagement</strong><small>Plans, repeat use, actions and resources accessed</small></li><li><strong>Service movement</strong><small>Referrals, warm handovers and meaningful journey milestones</small></li><li><strong>Outcomes</strong><small>Confidence, stability, wellbeing, progression and operational value</small></li><li><strong>Scale decision</strong><small>What to repeat, expand, integrate or stop next</small></li></ul>
          <a href="#book-a-call">Design a 2–5 member cohort <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section slot="after-solution" class="section ai-delivery-offer" id="ai-delivery-partnership" aria-labelledby="ai-delivery-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading audience-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow dark">Route 02 · AI Coaching &amp; Delivery Partnership</p><h2 id="ai-delivery-title">Add support capacity where people repeatedly need guidance and follow-through.</h2></div>
        <p>Bridgit can design and deploy AI coaches inside your own operations or partnership projects. Where the use case is not yet clear, a bounded Responsible AI diagnostic turns ambition into a safe go—or no-go—decision.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="corporate-usecase-grid">
        <article><span>Workforce</span><h3>Wellbeing, caring, money and progression</h3><p>Confidential guidance, planning and ongoing support that protects manager and specialist capacity.</p></article>
        <article><span>Projects &amp; contracts</span><h3>Jobs, skills and community outcomes</h3><p>Move people from awareness and referral into actions, appointments and measurable progression.</p></article>
        <article><span>Customers</span><h3>Vulnerability and service navigation</h3><p>Provide earlier, consistent support with safe handovers into the right human teams.</p></article>
        <article><span>Operations</span><h3>Policy, process and supplier guidance</h3><p>Reduce repeated explanations and give distributed teams one approved place to begin.</p></article>
        <article><span>Learning &amp; change</span><h3>Adoption and between-session action</h3><p>Keep people moving between workshops, training or transformation milestones.</p></article>
        <article><span>Community networks</span><h3>One approachable front door</h3><p>Scale local guidance across sites while retaining a clear route to human help.</p></article>
      </div>
      <div class="responsible-ai-path">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">A practical route to responsible deployment</p><h3>Diagnose. Pilot. Integrate. Scale.</h3><p>No generic AI strategy deck. We identify the real journey, ownership, boundaries, safeguards, measures and implementation route.</p></div>
        <ol><li><span>01</span><strong>Diagnostic</strong><small>Use case, users, workflow, data and safety owners</small></li><li><span>02</span><strong>Pilot</strong><small>Configured coach, baseline, governance and measures</small></li><li><span>03</span><strong>Integrate</strong><small>Workflow, CRM, outreach and reporting</small></li><li><span>04</span><strong>Scale</strong><small>More teams, sites, populations or contracts</small></li></ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</AudienceLanding>
